    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Urothelial carcinoma of the bladder, multifocal, with carcinoma in situ, pT2a pN0 (0 of 18 nodes), margins negative, treated by radical cystoprostatectomy with an ileal conduit; no evidence of disease; under surveillance; synthetic modern detail linked to his documented bladder cancer: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Ileal conduit urostomy, right lower abdomen: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Acquired absence of the bladder and part of the urethra after radical cystectomy: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Acquired absence of the prostate after cystoprostatectomy: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Personal history of pelvic radiation for bladder tumor, with earlier intravesical thiotepa: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Urology consultation to share survivorship surveillance after radical cystectomy, review the stoma, and set the metabolic monitoring plan. Guideline: Holzbeierlein J, et al. Treatment of Non-Metastatic Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer: AUA/ASCO/SUO Guideline (2017; Amended 2020, 2024). J Urol 2024;212(1):3-10 (2024); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Bladder Cancer (2026) [S]</item><item>Stoma care with the wound, ostomy, and continence nurse: appliance fitting, peristomal skin care, and parastomal hernia checks. Guideline: Holzbeierlein J, et al. Treatment of Non-Metastatic Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer: AUA/ASCO/SUO Guideline (2017; Amended 2020, 2024). J Urol 2024;212(1):3-10 (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, urologic cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Distress screening at each visit, physical activity, and a written survivorship care plan. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Bladder Cancer (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, urologic cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
